<comment>
Session 007 Part 1 canonical two-clump counterclockwise-orbit production input.

Agreed physical model: independently solved spherical Einstein-Vlasov envelope
M_source=0.76, areal radius R0=30, 3,000,000 particles; two Gaussian clumps each
M_source=0.12, sigma=0.70, s=0.02, 1,000,000 particles. The left clump at (-3,0,0)
has orthonormal beta_y=-0.0880124692901454 and the right clump at (+3,0,0) has
beta_y=+0.0880124692901454, giving counterclockwise orbital angular momentum.
This is the Session 006 envelope-only circular-geodesic prescription at isotropic
radius 3 (Omega=0.0244412311298025, P_env=257.073192173129), not exact binary
equilibrium. Approximate conformally flat boosted ID retain K_ij=0.

Inherited Arm-A method: RK4/CFL 0.4; alpha<0.05 particle removal; AH removal off;
strict measurement-only horizon acceptance; natural Lohner(alpha*psi^7, 0.2) AMR;
tracker_floor=false; physical dx_min=1/256. Two stable tagged trackers follow their
own cores, switch irreversibly to particle-independent lapse tracking after their
own accepted horizons, and persist predictor/identity state through checkpoints.
Individual AH candidates enclosing the other tracker are rejected. Finder 2 is a
strict, separately identified common-horizon search activated only at separation
below 4*(0.12+0.12)=0.96; only an accepted enclosing surface can establish merger.

Part-1 recommendation (not a previously approved endpoint): tlim=64, approximately
0.249 P_env. Domain [-256,256]^3, root dx=2, 8 root MeshBlocks per dimension,
logical root level 3. root-inclusive num_levels=10 gives physical levels 0..9,
logical levels 3..12, dx_min=1/256. The boundary-to-envelope margin is 226; even a
conservative sqrt(2) gauge-speed estimate reaches R=30 only after about 159.8,
well beyond t=64. No Session 006 removal-plateau early stop is authorized.

<job>
basename = s7_two_clump_ccw

<mesh>
nghost = 4
nx1 = 256
x1min = -256.0
x1max = 256.0
ix1_bc = outflow
ox1_bc = outflow
nx2 = 256
x2min = -256.0
x2max = 256.0
ix2_bc = outflow
ox2_bc = outflow
nx3 = 256
x3min = -256.0
x3max = 256.0
ix3_bc = outflow
ox3_bc = outflow

<meshblock>
nx1 = 32
nx2 = 32
nx3 = 32

<time>
evolution = dynamic
integrator = rk4
cfl_number = 0.4
nlim = 100000000
tlim = 64.0
ndiag = 50
stop_file = REQUEST_STOP
stop_check_every = 256

<mesh_refinement>
refinement = adaptive
num_levels = 10
max_nmb_per_rank = 320
ncycle_check = 16
refinement_interval = 16

<amr_criterion1>
method = user

<z4c_amr>
method = loehner
tracker_floor = false
loehner_variable = alp_psi7
loehner_threshold = 0.2
radius_0_rad = 34.0
radius_0_reflevel = 1
radius_1_rad = 18.0
radius_1_reflevel = 2
radius_2_rad = 15.0
radius_2_reflevel = 3

